      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4378727908858309690, guid: 34b3940e982d4fd4b8a073e83a19eed9, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_IsActive
      value: 0
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4529810050646013760, guid: 34b3940e982d4fd4b8a073e83a19eed9, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: Well done! Light is a form of energy, not matter. It has no mass and
        does not occupy space in the same way that matter does. Let's move onto the
        next object
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4563303506170522818, guid: 34b3940e982d4fd4b8a073e83a19eed9, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: Think about what you just observed and what you know about matter. Select
        the statements that correctly describe the mass and volume of light. T
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 4563303506170522818, guid: 34b3940e982d4fd4b8a073e83a19eed9, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_fontColor32.rgba
      value: 4278190080
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6412335047596291952, guid: 34b3940e982d4fd4b8a073e83a19eed9, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: This is the shadow cast by the cube. The cube blocks some of the light
        from the light source, so less light reaches this part of the table. The
        shadow shows where the light is blocked. The cube has mass and takes up space,
        but the shadow itself has no mass.
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 6412335047596291952, guid: 34b3940e982d4fd4b8a073e83a19eed9, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_fontColor32.rgba
